              PLPP3 encodes LPP3 (lipid phosphate phosphatase 3), a cell-surface
              enzyme that can regulate the availability of bioactive
              lysophopsholipids including lysophosphatidic acid (LPA). The
              protective allele of PLPP3 increases LPP3 expression during cell
              exposure to oxidized lipids, however, the role of LPP3 in
              atherosclerosis remains unclear. Approach and Results: In this
