  volume   =  6,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  74,
  abstract = "Abstract Complex tissue regeneration is extremely rare among adult
              mammals. An exception, however, is the superior tissue healing of
              multiple organs in spiny mice ( Acomys ). While Acomys species
              exhibit the remarkable ability to heal complex tissue with minimal
              scarring, little is known about their cardiac structure and
